---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About — Interlaced Pixel" description="Interlaced Pixel is an independent software studio building useful applications, systems software, and developer tools.">
	<header class="page-hero about-page-hero">
		<div class="container narrow reveal">
			<p class="kicker"><span></span> About Interlaced Pixel</p>
			<h1>A small studio<br><em>for serious software.</em></h1>
			<p>Interlaced Pixel is an independent software development studio in Baton Rouge, Louisiana. We build applications, systems software, and developer tools with a focus on clarity, performance, and dependable behavior.</p>
			<div class="button-row">
				<a href="/contact" class="button primary">Work with us <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
				<a href="/services" class="button secondary">What we do</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</header>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="container detail-grid about-principles">
			<div class="reveal">
				<p class="kicker">Our approach</p>
				<h2>Make the useful thing, and make it understandable.</h2>
				<p>We start by getting specific about the problem and the constraints. Then we choose a proportionate technical approach, keep progress visible, and deliver software that can be understood and maintained.</p>
			</div>
			<ul class="spec-list reveal">
				<li><span>Scope</span><strong>Focused on the real need</strong></li>
				<li><span>Engineering</span><strong>Performance and reliability considered early</strong></li>
				<li><span>Delivery</span><strong>Working software and clear handover</strong></li>
				<li><span>Location</span><strong>Baton Rouge, Louisiana</strong></li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-contrast">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-heading reveal">
				<div><p class="kicker light">How an engagement works</p><h2>Clear steps.<br>Useful checkpoints.</h2></div>
			</div>
			<ol class="engagement-grid">
				<li class="reveal"><span>01</span><h3>Talk through the problem</h3><p>We learn about the users, desired outcome, constraints, and what you already know.</p></li>
				<li class="reveal"><span>02</span><h3>Agree on a useful scope</h3><p>We identify the first deliverable, a practical approach, and how we’ll communicate progress.</p></li>
				<li class="reveal"><span>03</span><h3>Build and refine</h3><p>We share working progress, incorporate feedback, and address technical risks as they surface.</p></li>
				<li class="reveal"><span>04</span><h3>Deliver and support</h3><p>We hand over the result with the information needed to run, understand, and continue its development.</p></li>
			</ol>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section engagement-options-section">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-heading reveal">
				<div><p class="kicker">Ways to work together</p><h2>Start with the shape<br>of the problem.</h2></div>
				<p class="section-intro">The right format depends on what you need to learn or deliver first.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="engagement-options">
				<article class="reveal"><h3>Discovery or prototype</h3><p>Clarify the technical direction and test an idea before a larger commitment.</p></article>
				<article class="reveal"><h3>Defined project</h3><p>Build a specific feature, tool, or application with an agreed scope and delivery plan.</p></article>
				<article class="reveal"><h3>Ongoing development</h3><p>Continue improving software through a series of planned engineering increments.</p></article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="container reveal">
			<p class="kicker">Interlaced Pixel · Baton Rouge, Louisiana</p>
			<h2>Let’s make progress on your project.</h2>
			<a href="/contact" class="button light-button">Start a conversation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
